Here's how to create a user in Azure AD B2C with the extension_RequirePasswordChange attribute set using C# and the Microsoft Graph SDK:


---

Step 1: Prerequisites

1. Install the Microsoft Graph SDK:

dotnet add package Microsoft.Graph
dotnet add package Microsoft.Identity.Client


2. Set Up API Permissions:

Ensure your Azure AD B2C app registration has the required permissions:

User.ReadWrite.All

Directory.ReadWrite.All


Grant Admin Consent for these permissions.



3. Add the Custom Attribute:

Make sure the extension_RequirePasswordChange attribute is created in Azure AD B2C under User Attributes.





---

Step 2: C# Code to Create User with Custom Attribute

using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Microsoft.Graph;
using Azure.Identity;

class Program
{
    static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Initialize Graph client
        var tenantId = "<Your-Tenant-ID>";
        var clientId = "<Your-Client-ID>";
        var clientSecret = "<Your-Client-Secret>";

        var clientSecretCredential = new ClientSecretCredential(tenantId, clientId, clientSecret);
        var graphClient = new GraphServiceClient(clientSecretCredential);

        // Replace <AppId> with your Application ID (without dashes)
        var extensionName = "extension_<AppId>_RequirePasswordChange";

        // Create a new user
        var newUser = new User
        {
            AccountEnabled = true,
            DisplayName = "John Doe",
            MailNickname = "johndoe",
            UserPrincipalName = "johndoe@example.com", // Ensure the domain matches your B2C domain
            PasswordProfile = new PasswordProfile
            {
                ForceChangePasswordNextSignIn = false,
                Password = "TempPassword123!"
            },
            AdditionalData = new System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary<string, object>
            {
                { extensionName, true }
            }
        };

        try
        {
            var createdUser = await graphClient.Users
                .Request()
                .AddAsync(newUser);

            Console.WriteLine($"User created successfully. User ID: {createdUser.Id}");
        }
        catch (ServiceException ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"Error creating user: {ex.Message}");
        }
    }
}


---

Key Points in the Code

1. Custom Attribute Name:

Replace <AppId> with your Application ID from the app registration (formatted without dashes).

Example: If your Application ID is 12345678-abcd-1234-efgh-12345678abcd, the custom attribute name will be extension_12345678abcd_RequirePasswordChange.



2. Password Profile:

The ForceChangePasswordNextSignIn property should be false because Azure AD B2C doesn’t fully support it. Instead, we handle password changes via the custom attribute.



3. Additional Data:

Use the AdditionalData dictionary to include the custom attribute when creating the user.





---

Step 3: Test the Custom Policy

Ensure your Azure AD B2C custom policy is configured to check the extension_RequirePasswordChange attribute. If set to true, the user should be directed to a password reset or change flow.


---

Expected Outcome

The user is created in Azure AD B2C with the extension_RequirePasswordChange attribute set to true.

During login, the user is redirected to a password reset or change screen based on the custom policy.


